# Advisory exceptions for govulncheck. Enforced by scripts/govulncheck-check.sh.
#
# Format, one entry per line:
#
#   <GO-YYYY-NNNN>  <expiry YYYY-MM-DD>  <reason to end of line>
#
# An entry suppresses exactly ONE advisory until its expiry date. After that
# the gate fails until the entry is renewed in a reviewed diff — an exception
# cannot persist unattended, which is what stops this file becoming a
# graveyard of forgotten risk.
#
# Only reach for an entry when the advisory has NO released fix. If a fix
# exists, bump the dependency instead:
#
#   cd apps/api && go get <module>@<fixed-version> && go mod tidy
#
# A malformed line, an expired entry, or an entry for an advisory that no
# longer appears all fail the gate deliberately. See
# specs/domains/platform-operations.md for the runbook.
#
# Empty is the expected steady state.
